**Findings**

The camera ray does not use `CollisionWorld`’s cell-extent path. `FreeChaseCamera` calls `ClientWorld::collide`, which enters [ClientWorld.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/core/ClientWorld.cpp:794). For a non-world cell, `internalCollide()` collides against `cellProperty->getOwner()` and then recurses through portals; it does not call `CollisionWorld::queryInteraction()` or `CellProperty::getCollisionExtent()`.

The actual wall surface available to this camera query is the **cell appearance object**:
- Cell baselines call `portalProperty->cellLoaded(..., true)` in [CellObject.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/object/CellObject.cpp:125).
- `PortalProperty::cellLoaded()` initializes the cell in [PortalProperty.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/portal/PortalProperty.cpp:474).
- `CellProperty::initialize(..., createAppearance=true)` creates `"Cell appearance object"`, attaches it as a child of the cell owner, and loads `cellTemplate.getAppearanceName()` in [CellProperty.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/portal/CellProperty.cpp:417).
- `ClientWorld::internalCollideObject()` walks child objects when `CF_childObjects` is set, which `CF_allCamera` includes, in [ClientWorld.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/core/ClientWorld.cpp:1330) and [ClientWorld.h](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/core/ClientWorld.h:59).

`CF_interiorGeometry` is effectively not a separate camera-data source in this path. It is defined in [ClientWorld.h](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/core/ClientWorld.h:47), but the `ClientWorld::collide()` implementation does not branch on it to test `CellProperty::getCollisionExtent()`. The cell collision extent exists and is loaded from `.pob` cell `0005` data at [PortalPropertyTemplate.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/portal/PortalPropertyTemplate.cpp:777), exposed through [CellProperty.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/portal/CellProperty.cpp:959), but that explicit cell-extent path is used by `CollisionWorld::queryInteraction()` at [CollisionWorld.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/shared/library/sharedCollision/src/shared/core/CollisionWorld.cpp:1359), not by the chase camera.

For the cell appearance to collide, its mesh primitives must build collision data:
- `MeshAppearance::collide()` requires an extent and then delegates to `ShaderPrimitiveSet::collide()` in [MeshAppearance.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/library/clientObject/src/shared/appearance/MeshAppearance.cpp:343).
- `ShaderPrimitiveSetTemplate::collisionSplit()` builds collision triangle data only if the shader template is collidable or opaque-solid in [ShaderPrimitiveSetTemplate.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/library/clientGraphics/src/shared/ShaderPrimitiveSetTemplate.cpp:863).
- Runtime collision also checks `CollideParameters::cms_default` type against `isCollidable()` / `isOpaqueSolid()` at [ShaderPrimitiveSetTemplate.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/library/clientGraphics/src/shared/ShaderPrimitiveSetTemplate.cpp:1400) and [CollideParameters.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/shared/library/sharedCollision/src/shared/core/CollideParameters.cpp:86).

OURS vs REFERENCE on this path:
- Portal/cell appearance registration path is effectively the same. The only portal `CellProperty` diff I found is our interior-layout throttle cursor, which affects lazy client-only placed layout objects, not cell wall appearance creation.
- `ClientInteriorLayoutManager` differs for throttled furniture/layout creation, not wall geometry.
- `sharedObject/src/shared/appearance` had no diff.
- `clientGraphics` does differ substantially. That matters because wall collision data is shader-dependent. If OUR active renderer/config causes the cell wall shader’s active implementation to be absent or reports not-collidable/not-opaque, `collisionSplit()` will not create collision data, and the camera ray will have no wall triangle to hit. The relevant active shader chain is [ShaderEffect.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/library/clientGraphics/src/shared/ShaderEffect.cpp:173), [StaticShaderTemplate.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/library/clientGraphics/src/shared/StaticShaderTemplate.cpp:213), and D3D11 reports legacy shader capability `2.0` at [Direct3d11.cpp](/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11.cpp:223).

Plain answer: in OUR tree, `ClientWorld::collide(... CF_allCamera)` can hit an interior wall only if the cell appearance child exists and its mesh/shader path built collidable triangle data. It does **not** independently hit `.pob` cell collision extents via `CF_interiorGeometry`. If the camera passes through a POB wall while REFERENCE does not, the strongest source-level suspect is not camera code but missing/non-collidable **cell appearance mesh collision data**, likely from renderer/shader capability/config/asset selection. The fix should live in that data-registration path, or in adding a real `CF_interiorGeometry` cell-extent test to `ClientWorld::internalCollide()` for non-world cells.
